## 7. PRIVACY & SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

- No `INTERNET` permission; no network libraries; no analytics. `android:allowBackup="false"` (or strictly configured backup rules excluding vault/DB).
- Keep three ideas separate in code and UI: **processing locally**, **storing locally**, **transmitting externally** (the last is impossible by design). Default = store minimum.
- Room DB + vault payloads encrypted with AES-256-GCM, key in Android Keystore (non-exportable), per-record random IV. Optional biometric/device-credential gate for Vault and Export. `FLAG_SECURE` on Vault/Result screens (optional toggle).
- Safe parsing of all inputs (malformed URLs, huge strings, control characters). Never execute/open scanned content.
- Permissions requested **only when the feature is used**, with a plain-language rationale first: camera (QR), notifications (alerts), SMS (optional auto-scan). Image picking uses the system photo picker (no storage permission).
- Notifications hide content on lock screen by default.
- "Delete all data" wipes DB, files, DataStore, keys.
- `docs/PRIVACY.md` documents all data, where it lives, and how to delete it.

