## 11. EDGE CASES (all must be handled gracefully)

No indicators → Low risk, *not guaranteed safe* · very short text → "insufficient context" · suspicious URL inside otherwise normal text → analyse URL separately · unsupported language → limited-analysis warning · spelling mistakes/paraphrases → still analysed (normalisation + fuzzy match) · mixed languages → supported · unreadable/encrypted text → ask for readable content · legitimate but urgent message → don't treat urgency as proof · genuine bank URL + suspicious request → analyse content and URL independently · extremely long input → truncate with notice · rule files missing/corrupt → show "detector unavailable", **never pretend analysis succeeded** · OCR returns nothing → say so and let the user type text.

